# Multi-subject — M2a CamelCase dual-subject (trigger HDP new path)
#
# Companion to m1a/m1b. Those two cases passed but the new HDP
# multi-subject branch did NOT fire because:
#   - m1a: LLM emit is_relational_lookup=false → no relation hyp
#   - m1a/m1b: entities were multi-word phrases ("explorer agent"),
#     normalizer dual-gate A failed for standalone kindEnWord
#     surfaces → topSymbols returned ≤1 → single-subject path
#
# This case picks TWO exported CamelCase identifiers so the
# normalizer's kindCamel branch (canonicalize.go:52-75) bypasses the
# dual-gate entirely and lands both as TermSymbol with Confidence≥0.9.
# topSymbols must return ≥2, which forces Plan into the multi-subject
# `default` branch → explainSetHypothesis fires with Statement
# "anchored on the set {Criterion, Hypothesis}". The literal
# substring "anchored on the set" in the log confirms the new path.
#
# Ground truth:
#   Criterion (internal/types/analysis_ir.go:464) — 2-field struct
#     {Kind, Expr}, the closed namespace lives at lines 476-495.
#     Consumed by criterion.Eval (dispatch), gate.checkCriterionResolvable
#     (registration check), stopcond.ShouldStop (OR-ed eval),
#     scheduler EntryConditions, AcceptanceTests.
#   Hypothesis (internal/types/analysis_ir.go:616) — 6 fields incl.
#     RequiredEvidence []Criterion + FalsificationCondition Criterion,
#     i.e. Hypothesis is the Criterion-container. Produced by
#     hdp.Plan, bound by binder, verdicted via emit_hypothesis_verdict.
#
# The relationship is structural: Hypothesis *contains* Criterion.
# EXPECT_SECTIONS enforces symmetry; EXPECT_CONTAINS pins the fact
# that Hypothesis embeds Criterion lists.
ID="m2a"
NAME="dual-subject CamelCase — Criterion and Hypothesis roles"
QUESTION="codrax 的 AnalysisIR 里 Criterion 和 Hypothesis 这两个结构体分别承担什么角色？各自有哪些字段？两者在结构上是什么关系？"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="Criterion Hypothesis RequiredEvidence FalsificationCondition"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS=".java .py identical same.struct"
EXPECT_SECTIONS="Criterion Hypothesis"
